## Separate, still-open issue: Cloudflare cache (lower priority, deferred)
Cloudflare Cache Rule "cache html pages" (rule order 2, all incoming requests)
is set to **"Ignore cache-control header and use this TTL" = 1 month** — meaning
Cloudflare completely ignores Vercel's own Cache-Control headers on ALL HTML and
blindly serves edge-cached HTML for up to 30 days regardless of redeploys. This
was flagged as a real staleness/rollback risk (fixes/deploys invisible to visitors
for up to a month) but the user pivoted to focus on function size first. Recommended
fix when revisited: change that rule's Edge TTL to "Use cache-control header if
present, cache request with Cloudflare's default TTL for the response status if
not" (i.e., respect origin) — but do this only AFTER the function-size /
ISR-revalidation settings are sane, not before (respecting origin will cause more
requests to reach Vercel to check freshness, which interacts with revalidation
frequency/cost). User mentioned "3.6 million monthly revalidation reads" during
this session but clarified afterward this was not meant as a real reported number
to investigate — treat as a red herring / miscommunication, not a lead.

